messages:
Ava M.: Heads-up: we need the final benchmark narrative + assets for next Wednesday. Primary story: how serving configs (hosted vs dedicated vs quantized) change real $/request and SLA tail risk. Two deliverables: a short hero claim for social and a blog hero + two charts (one standalone for social, one composite for the blog).
Samir P.: Got it. Two headline directions: (1) "Serve smarter, spend less" and (2) "Lower bills without swapping models". Short social riffs: "Serve smarter, spend less" -> "Serve smarter = lower spend"; "Lower bills without swapping models" -> "Same model. Lower cost."
Ava M.: Nice. Keep both; we'll A/B test social headlines. Also need 2 subhead variants (dev-focused vs finance-focused).
Samir P.: Draft subs: dev: "Optimize serving to hit latency SLAs while cutting token spend"; finance: "Reduce inference spend per 1k tokens without sacrificing latency SLAs"
Jen O.: Data we can use: p50 latency (hosted) = 95ms, p95 = 360ms; dedicated fastpath p50 = 70ms, p95 = 220ms. Dedicated throughput ~5k tokens/s under typical batch mix. Median request length = 54 tokens. Inference-only cost per 1k tokens: naive pipeline $0.0120, optimized $0.0045, quantized variant $0.0032. That implies ~2.67x saving naive->optimized and ~3.75x naive->quantized.
Elena G.: Visual plan: 1) standalone social card: big stat + microchart (cost per 1k tokens) + CTA; 2) blog composite (two rows): top row waterfall cost breakdown (model compute, batching efficiency, KV cache savings), bottom row latency tail scatter: x-axis = cost-per-1k, y-axis = p95 latency by serving profile. Use redwood palette (deep blue, teal, charcoal) and clear microcopy.
Noah B.: For inbound routing: use tags bench-inquiry and enterprise-interest. Rule idea: if lead.estimated_monthly_tokens >= 150000000 OR lead.ARR_usd >= 1000000 -> sales-enterprise; else -> growth-led. Also prefer company_size >= 50 as tie-breaker for SDR assign.
Ravi C.: Routing snippet for staging (copyable):
```
if (lead.tags.includes('bench-inquiry')) {
  if (lead.estimated_monthly_tokens >= 150000000 || lead.ARR_usd >= 1000000) {
    tag('enterprise-interest'); assign('sales-enterprise');
  } else if (lead.company_size >= 50) {
    assign('sdr');
  } else {
    assign('growth-led');
  }
}
```
Elena G.: For the waterfall, please give me the percentage buckets: model compute 68%, batching/throughput savings 18%, cache/prefix 14% (these add nuance visually). Add tiny caption: "Normalized inference-only costs; excludes infra, data, and storage."
Jen O.: Add to copy: median cost per typical request (54 tokens) drops from ~$0.00065 -> ~$0.00024 (naive -> optimized) — present both per-request and per-1k tokens for clarity.
Ava M.: Good. Samir, include the per-request and per-1k numbers in both subheads and the social captions. Also provide 3 CTAs: "Run your benchmark", "Try the cost calculator", "Book a latency review".
Samir P.: I'll deliver: 2 headline families, 2 subheads each (dev + finance), 3 social captions, 3 CTAs, and short alt text for the images by COB today.
Noah B.: Webinar: 25-min technical deep dive + 20-min Q&A. Form will ask for estimated monthly tokens and role (engineering, infra, finance) to improve routing. :rocket:
routing-bot: Routing rule created in staging under 'bench-inquiry' namespace. Use /deploy-route when ready to push to prod.
Ava M.: Timeline: copy in Slack by 5pm; Elena to mock visuals tonight; quick review tomorrow 11am. Thanks team! :thumbsup:
